      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was founded March 5, 1794 as one of the earliest townships of the Military Tract and named after Roman general Scipio.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofscipiony.gov/about",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the late 1800s, railroads turned Scipio into a hub for social reform, hosting abolitionists, the Underground Railroad, and early women’s rights activists.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofscipiony.gov/about",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Jethro Wood’s 1819 iron plow invention helped turn Scipio’s virgin forests into productive farmland, spurring a boom in farming enterprises.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofscipiony.gov/about",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Ensenore Glen Hotel on Owasco Lake drew vacationers in the 1800s, where they could dine, sail, swim, and watch a 1878 rowing contest between Cornell and Harvard.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofscipiony.gov/about",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 2011 the Town of Scipio adopted a Comprehensive Plan, followed by new subdivision and zoning rules in 2015 to guide modern growth.",
